  "ring": {
    "_note": "The one tower menu: a radial ring of icon buttons around the pad or tower, and a description panel beside it. Every number is in CSS pixels and stays that size at every camera zoom — the ring is HUD chrome positioned by projecting a world point, not a world object.",
    "buttonSize": 50,
    "_buttonSize": "The plate. iconSize is the floor, not this: 40px of icon needs a plate bigger than 40 to sit on, and 50 leaves a 5px border. It is not larger because a notched 568x320 leaves a 171px strip between the counters and the ability bar, and six options need 2*50 plus the price badge inside it. The exhaustive placement test pinned that number down.",
    "iconSize": 40,
    "_iconSize": "Never below 40. Under it the 256px source is minified past 6x and the painted outlines break up — the same failure the whole cast had before rule 7 was restated in physical pixels.",
    "buttonGap": 10,
    "priceGap": 3,
    "priceHeight": 17,
    "priceSize": 15,
    "minRadius": 62,
    "panelGap": 14,
    "areaMargin": 4,
    "panelWidth": 226,
    "_panelWidth": "Fixed. Text wraps into it; the panel never widens to fit a long name, because a panel whose width depends on its content moves the confirm button between towers.",
    "panelMaxHeightFraction": 0.92,
    "titleSize": 16,
    "bodySize": 14,
    "rowSize": 14,
    "rowHeight": 18,
    "bodyMinSize": 11,
    "_bodyMinSize": "The floor the description shrinks to. Below this it is not small text, it is a grey smear on a phone. If the content still does not fit at this size the panel SAYS SO rather than clipping.",
    "confirmHeight": 46,
    "pad": 11,
    "maxAspect": 2.2,
    "_maxAspect": "The HUD leaves a wide, short strip — 824x210 on the reference phone — and a circle big enough to keep six plates apart is 242px in both directions. The ring stretches sideways into the room that is actually there, up to this, and no further: past it the ring stops reading as a ring and starts reading as a row.",
    "rowMinHeight": 14,
    "_rowMinHeight": "Stat rows tighten with the description when a panel is too tall. A support tower spends more height on rows than on prose, so shrinking only the prose is not enough of a lever.",
    "headerIconSize": 26,
    "_headerIconSize": "The picture at the top of the description panel, so the player can see which ring button they are reading about. Smaller than iconSize deliberately: that 40px floor is for buttons a thumb has to hit, and this one is not pressed. The 14px it gives back is the difference between the panel fitting a notched phone and reporting that it does not.",
    "_confirmHeight": "Tall enough to actually carry a 40px icon. It was 38, which is shorter than the icon standing on it — the floor is a floor, and a plate that cannot hold it is the plate that has to grow.",
    "titleMinSize": 13,
    "_titleMinSize": "The title gives way last, because it is what a player reads first — but two lines of 16px title is 40px of a 238px budget on the smallest phone."
  }
